From 8cc7cc4bfa948222df1a01639b78ba648cc6e8ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Esther Ngulu <esther.ngulu@standardbank.com.na>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:56:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] feat: add multi-database support (SQL Server,
 PostgreSQL, SQLite)

- Create DatabaseSettings config model for provider selection
- Implement DbContextFactory with provider-specific configuration
- Add DesignTimeDbContextFactory for EF Core migrations
- Update Program.cs to support dynamic provider selection at startup
- Register provider-specific health checks (SQL Server, PostgreSQL, SQLite)
- Add NuGet packages: Npgsql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgreSQL, Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite
- Update appsettings.json with connection strings for all three providers
- Create initial migration for multi-database setup
- Enable switching between databases via appsettings configuration

Single migration set - EF Core generates provider-specific SQL automatically.
Configurable at startup - select database in appsettings.json before running.

Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
